{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWJvwQNxGvNhPj2Go85UHu","type":"tool_result","content":"68:- 615 10k. Save slots; E.Saves: saves\n69:- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n70:- 711 Blob rig; E.Blob: blob\n101:- 1590 Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js); E.World: world\n162:- `E.hash2(x, y)`: a fixed random number 0..1 for whole-number grid coordinates (texture specks, scatter that never flickers)\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and appl\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a bloc\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, d\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu(\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the da\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from \n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, h\n708:- `E.knockback(from, target, speed = 160, up = 0)`: push a target away from a point (attacker): uses target.push (E.Body) or its vx / vy. up = upward speed (knock into the air)\n713:- `new E.Blob(o = {}) → blob`: new E.Blob({ R: 6.5, colors, ears, horns, wings, feet, tail, mouth, face }): a squash-and-stretch rig for slimes and jellies; blob.update(dt, state) each step, blob.draw(g, ox, oy, view) in an r.\n760:- `map.los(x0, y0, x1, y1)`: line of sight across the ground (true if nothing solid in between). It ignores heights: sight() is the one that sees over a low wall and from a roof\n766:- `map.sight(a, b, o = {})`: can a's eyes (z + eye) see b's chest (z + chest)? E.HEIGHTS gives both unless o ({ eye, target }) or the bodies' own eye and chest say otherwise. A guard sees over a planter lower than its eyes, an\n836:- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191741__x8b64cc/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0729cc04-0deb-412e-a406-b462eee591a2","uuid":"46265762-b467-40b0-a180-656b7bc4ed6f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:19:50.299Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"68:- 615 10k. Save slots; E.Saves: saves\n69:- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n70:- 711 Blob rig; E.Blob: blob\n101:- 1590 Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js); E.World: world\n162:- `E.hash2(x, y)`: a fixed random number 0..1 for whole-number grid coordinates (texture specks, scatter that never flickers)\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and appl\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a bloc\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, d\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu(\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the da\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from \n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, h\n708:- `E.knockback(from, target, speed = 160, up = 0)`: push a target away from a point (attacker): uses target.push (E.Body) or its vx / vy. up = upward speed (knock into the air)\n713:- `new E.Blob(o = {}) → blob`: new E.Blob({ R: 6.5, colors, ears, horns, wings, feet, tail, mouth, face }): a squash-and-stretch rig for slimes and jellies; blob.update(dt, state) each step, blob.draw(g, ox, oy, view) in an r.\n760:- `map.los(x0, y0, x1, y1)`: line of sight across the ground (true if nothing solid in between). It ignores heights: sight() is the one that sees over a low wall and from a roof\n766:- `map.sight(a, b, o = {})`: can a's eyes (z + eye) see b's chest (z + chest)? E.HEIGHTS gives both unless o ({ eye, target }) or the bodies' own eye and chest say otherwise. A guard sees over a planter lower than its eyes, an\n836:- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191741__x8b64cc/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UWJvwQNxGvNhPj2Go85UHu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
