ead it in pieces.\",\n    \"I would overhaul the spatial helpers' return types: one shape everywhere, {x, y}, instead of arrays for center() and objects for find().\",\n    \"I would change one thing: ship the engine as a smaller bundle for simple games. The 1.2 MB engine makes the single-file page about 1.3 MB.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"I liked the explicit done-conditions, the list of screens that must exist, and the exit-interview shape: they made the finish line clear.\",\n    \"Confusing: 'create a subfolder here' and 'bundle into the root' used 'here' and 'root' for different places, and 'usage only if estimates are available' sat next to 'answer every field'. Silently brainstorming 50 titles while also needing a real RNG pick was hard to square.\",\n    \"The hardest thing was fitting every listed feature (attract mode, hub round, gamepad inversion, Xbox symbols, touch-only, about and credits) into one session on a large engine.\",\n    \"The test I would most want run: the real hub harness with two browser tabs in parallel mode, plus a simulated Gamepad API to check the inversion settings.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"BREAKING DUST BOWL\",\n    \"tagline\": \"A bad batch in a dry town\",\n    \"description\": \"A top-down desert crime story with a timed cook, a sneak-and-deliver run past Vail's men, and a telegraphed showdown in a chapel ruin.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Adventure\",\n    \"source\": \"Breaking Bad (2008-2013)\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or WASD move; J, X or click swings; Space dashes; Enter or Space confirms\",\n    \"tags\": [\"top-down\", \"comedy\", \"boss fights\", \"exploration\", \"retro\", \"desert\"]\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1,"newLines":6,"lines":[" {","   \"sourceInformation\": {","-    \"date\": \"2026-11-02 19:27\",","+    \"date\": \"2026-11-02 19:38\",","     \"source\": \"Breaking Bad (20