{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfDJ67gkjabZSxkdRqrw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017A3sJcdii8d6zcizDJu4Ua","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/exit-interview.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"Six game issues: the desert never spawned its batches (a map helper returned arrays where the code read x and y); the desert AI walked into rocks; the showdown crashed for lack of a flow field; the title menu covered the lineup; the lineup ran off-screen after that fix; the touch-only message never showed. Three test-harness mistakes (a stale progress state, a promise not flushed, back-to-back presses) were mine and are not counted.\",\n \"Two were critical: the batches never spawning (the desert could not be played) and the showdown crash (it stopped the attract run). The stuck AI blocked the attract run too, but it did not break play.\",\n \"Most helpful: the headless attract run, which plays the lab, desert and showdown with the error log open. It caught the spawn bug, the stuck AI and the showdown crash.\",\n \"Least helpful: the hub stub test. It checks the calls I wrote against a stub of my own, not the real hub. Its one failure was my own timing, not a game bug.\"\n]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False); open(p,'a').write('\\n')\nprint(len(d['testingFeedback']), len(d['engineFeedback']), len(d['promptFeedback']))\nEOF\nnode build.mjs && node -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8')); console.log('parses; keys', Object.keys(j).join(','), '; testing', j.testingFeedback.length, 'engine', j.engineFeedback.length, 'prompt', j.promptFeedback.length)\"","description":"Rewrite testing feedback as four ordered answers and rebuild"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_cr